# Build context for docker/Dockerfile.api: default deny, then only what the API
# image needs. The data and artifact files are the ones the API opens, measured
# with `python -m med_deploy reads` (docs/phase_9/LOCAL_DEPLOYMENT.md). Never in
# the image: .git, .venv, private local notes, var and any local feedback, tests,
# docs, secrets, the superseded v1/v2 baseline data and artifacts, and every file
# that stores frozen test outcomes.
*
!constraints.txt
!pyproject.toml
!src
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
src/*.egg-info
# Of the deployment-check package, the images need only the bundle check and the
# environment report (both run at build time and by hand). The other modules
# drive checks from the host and stay out, so editing one does not change an image.
src/med_deploy/*
!src/med_deploy/__init__.py
!src/med_deploy/__main__.py
!src/med_deploy/bundle.py
!src/med_deploy/cli.py
!src/med_deploy/environment.py
!src/med_deploy/version.py
!data/med-synth-v4
!artifacts/med-features-v2
!artifacts/med-model-v2/model.joblib
!artifacts/med-policy-v2/policy.json
# Bind-mounted by the build's bundle check only (the Dockerfile does not copy it).
!artifacts/med-deploy-v1/bundle_digests.json
